menu "Omega Stick Configuration"

config OMEGA_STICK_BOOT_FLASH_WINDOW_S
    int "Seconds to wait at boot before starting USB"
    default 0
    range 0 60
    help
      Development aid. Until the firmware starts TinyUSB, the ESP32-S3's
      built-in USB Serial/JTAG still owns the USB port, so `idf.py flash`
      can reset the board into the bootloader without holding BOOT.

      Set this in menuconfig (15 works well) to open that window on every
      boot. Your local sdkconfig is gitignored, so the setting stays on your
      machine. Leave it at 0 for anything users run: they would wait this
      long before the stick responds.

config OMEGA_STICK_OTA
    bool "Firmware updates over USB"
    default y
    help
      On by default. The calibration console can install new firmware over
      USB, and a new image must be confirmed by the console or the board
      reverts to the previous one.

      Turn it off to build without the update engine and the post-update
      health check: the console's firmware update messages then reply
      function_not_supported, and new firmware is installed from the
      first-flash page. Use the sdkconfig.no_ota defaults fragment, or
      menuconfig.

      The bootloader and partition table are the same either way.

endmenu
